ision of thought new to comics and rare in any medium. Mausties together two powerful stories: Vladek's harrowing take of survival against all odds, delineating the paradox of family life in the death camps, and the author's account of his tortured relationship with his aging father. At every level this is the ultimate survivor's tale-and that too of the children who somehow survive even the survivors.\"","publicationYear":1991,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times bestseller","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-maus-ii-art-spiegelman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"nyt:paperback_graphic_books=2012-01-07","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-maus-ii-art-spiegelman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United States","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-maus-ii-art-spiegelman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-maus-ii-art-spiegelman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Poland","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-maus-ii-art-spiegelman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Holocaust, Jewish (1939-1945)","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-maus-ii-art-spiegelman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Holocaust survivors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-maus-ii-art-spiegelman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Comic books, strips","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-maus-ii-art-spiegelman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Children of Holocaust survivors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-maus-ii-art-spiegelman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Holocaust, Jewish (1939-1945) fast (OCoLC)fst00958866","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-